# Docs languages

Every docs page outside the Developer reference ships in **English** and
**Simplified Chinese** (`zh-Hans`). This includes Intro, Quick start,
Concepts, Components, Design patterns, and Use cases. The navbar language
control (top right) persists the choice in `localStorage` (`docs-locale`) and
cookie `superdurable-docs-locale`.

The Developer reference is **English only**. It means the versioned
`reference-*` docs instances and the generated API references. When a page
moves into the Developer reference, it drops its Chinese copy. Redirect the old
`zh-Hans` URL like any other moved page; see
`.cursor/rules/docs-search-indexing.mdc`.

When you add or change a bilingual page under `docs/content/`:

1. Write English in `docs/content/...`.
2. Write Chinese at the same relative path under
   `docs/i18n/zh-Hans/docusaurus-plugin-content-docs/current/`.
3. Keep Dex terms untranslated: Flow, Step, Attribute, Channel, RPC, Timer.
4. Keep code samples identical across locales.
5. Do not ship a new English page without its Chinese counterpart.
6. Do not translate sidebar labels. Every Chinese page must set `sidebar_label`
   to the exact English label from its matching page. Use that page's English
   title when it has no `sidebar_label`.

Do not remove the locale switcher or the stored preference.
